Problem: a quiz app needs: the quiz title, the total number of questions (fixed at 10), the current question number (starts at 1, increases), the score (starts at 0, increases), and the pass mark (60%). Declare all variables with the best keyword and naming, then simulate answering two questions correctly and print `Question 3 of 10 - Score: 2`.

TRY FIRST.

SOLUTION
```javascript
const quizTitle = "JS Basics";
const TOTAL_QUESTIONS = 10;
const PASS_PERCENT = 60;
let currentQuestion = 1;
let score = 0;

score = score + 1;  currentQuestion = currentQuestion + 1;   // answered Q1 correctly
score = score + 1;  currentQuestion = currentQuestion + 1;   // answered Q2 correctly

console.log("Question", currentQuestion, "of", TOTAL_QUESTIONS, "- Score:", score);
```
Explanation: two configuration constants, one fixed string, two pieces of changing state. Follow-up: "What would break if `score` were `const`?" → TypeError on the first `score = score + 1`.

