### 13. DAY-END REVISION

□ A variable is a named container for a value
□ `var`: function-scoped, redeclarable, hoisted as `undefined`
□ `let`: block-scoped, reassignable, not redeclarable, TDZ
□ `const`: block-scoped, not reassignable, must be initialized, TDZ
□ Declaration vs initialization; `undefined` default
□ Reassignment (`x = ...`) vs redeclaration (`let x = ...` again)
□ Naming rules (letters, digits, `_`, `$`; no leading digit; case sensitive; no reserved words) and camelCase
□ Global scope, block scope; inner sees outer, not vice versa
□ Shadowing with `let` vs overwriting with `var`
□ Hoisting and TDZ at awareness level
□ Default `const`, `let` when reassigning, avoid `var`

